###############################################################################
# Part 5.3 - List Agent Identities belonging to the mapped Blueprint
#
# Expected: 200. The server-side filter uses the locked Blueprint appId.
# Read every returned page and verify every result's agentIdentityBlueprintId
# still equals that appId. Do not use a cached count or only the local source
# mapping.
#
# Before sending this request, acquire the Blueprint-group onboarding exclusion
# across every writer and restore path. If that exclusion cannot prevent a new
# child Identity or creation reservation, block cleanup. Drain every
# already-accepted create or restore operation to a terminal result; any
# unresolved operation must remain represented as a reservation.

# @name deleteListBlueprintAgentIdentities
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity?$filter=agentIdentityBlueprintId%20eq%20'{{blueprintAppId}}'&$select=id,agentIdentityBlueprintId
Authorization: Bearer {{deleteToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 5.3
#
# Save every page:
# ../../evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/agent-identities-before-blueprint-cleanup-page-1.json
# ../../evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/agent-identities-before-blueprint-cleanup-page-2.json
#
# Before treating the count as complete:
# - confirm the Blueprint-group onboarding exclusion remained held;
# - confirm every @odata.nextLink page was read;
# - count other active Agent Identities whose agentIdentityBlueprintId equals
#   A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID;
# - count active, pending, unresolved, or timed-out identity-creation
#   reservations for this Blueprint in the mapping journal; and
# - apply the configured directory-visibility interval and repeat the complete
#   scan; require both scans to produce the same Blueprint-bound counts unless
#   a stronger documented consistent-read mechanism is available; and
# - keep the onboarding exclusion until Blueprint deletion finishes or the
#   decision is to retain it.
#
# An incomplete enumeration, unavailable mapping journal, or failed exclusion
# must block cleanup. It must never be represented as zero.

###############################################################################
# Automatic Blueprint membership decision
#
# The reconciler now records the number of other active or pending Agent
# Identities and pending creation reservations assigned to this Blueprint.
# In production, the reconciler calculates both counts automatically from the
# complete filtered API response and the mapping/operation journal. It also
# supplies the enumeration-complete and onboarding-exclusion-held assertions.
# None of these values is a human approval gate.
#
# This manual experiment passes the saved evidence values as CLI arguments
# because the local prototype does not call Graph or the operation journal.
# Replace all angle-bracket values with the verified local evidence values:
#
# python demos/03-delete-companion/prototype_retirement_mapping.py `
#   --mapping evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   --output evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   event blueprint-membership-observed `
#   --blueprint-id "<exact-mapped-blueprint-app-id>" `
#   --remaining-agent-identities <verified-active-count> `
#   --pending-identity-reservations <verified-reservation-count> `
#   --enumeration-complete `
#   --onboarding-exclusion-held
#
# When either count is greater than zero:
# - keep blueprintCleanup.status=active;
# - require blueprintCleanup.reason=group-not-empty; and
# - stop Part 5 without another human decision.
#
# When the verified count is zero, continue automatically only when:
# - lifecycleStatus is retired;
# - the mapped Agent Identity is already retired;
# - the Blueprint and principal IDs match the locked mapping;
# - retirementApprovedAt is populated; and
# - both Blueprint object states are pending, with no unresolved block; and
# - blueprintCleanup.status is pending with reason
#   group-empty-automatic-cleanup.

###############################################################################
# Authentication 3 - Request a Blueprint cleanup device code
#
# Do not reuse a token that lacks AgentIdentityBlueprint.DeleteRestore.All.
# Never save this response. Stop rather than approve unexpected permissions.

# @name deleteBlueprintStartDeviceCode
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{clientId}}&scope={{blueprintDeleteScopes}}

###

###############################################################################
# Authentication 4 - Exchange the Blueprint cleanup device code
#
# Never save this response.

# @name deleteBlueprintToken
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Adevice_code&client_id={{clientId}}&device_code={{deleteBlueprintStartDeviceCode.response.body.$.device_code}}

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED REVALIDATION BEFORE PART 5.4
#
# Repeat Part 5.3 and the `blueprint-membership-observed` event immediately
# before DELETE. If authentication or another delay interrupted the onboarding
# exclusion, reacquire it first and discard the earlier zero-count evidence.
# Continue only with a fresh zero/zero result bound to the same Blueprint ID.
#
# Immediately before sending DELETE, persist that an approved destructive
# request is about to be issued:
#
# python demos/03-delete-companion/prototype_retirement_mapping.py `
#   --mapping evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   --output evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   event blueprint-delete-started
#
# If DELETE then times out or its response is lost, do not rebuild pre-delete
# eligibility merely to verify the outcome. Read the exact Blueprint ID first.
# A verified 404 completes the pending delete phase. A 200 requires fresh
# membership evidence before retrying DELETE. Any Blueprint or principal block
# also prevents the initial DELETE or a retry until it is explicitly resolved
# and fresh eligibility is recorded.

###############################################################################
# Part 5.4 - Automatic empty-Blueprint soft deletion
#
# Expected: 204. The action runner uses the existing retirement approval and
# the typed endpoint's AgentIdentityBlueprint.DeleteRestore.All permission.
