###############################################################################
# Part 5.6 - Observe Blueprint principal cascade deletion
#
# Expected eventually: 404.
#
# The observed Graph 404 may use the generic message:
#
# "Resource '' does not exist or one of its queried reference-property
# objects are not present."
#
# The empty quotes are an unpopulated resource label in Graph's
# alternate-key/type-cast error template; they do not by themselves mean that
# blueprintAppId was empty. Treat this as the expected absence result only
# when the HTTP status is 404, the error code is Request_ResourceNotFound,
# blueprintAppId is still populated, and the same locked appId resolved the
# principal successfully before Blueprint deletion.
#
# A 200 means cascade cleanup has not completed. Save the observation, leave
# blueprintPrincipal.status=pending, wait, and repeat this GET. Do not send a
# separate principal DELETE merely to make the experiment complete.

# @name deleteGetBlueprintPrincipalAfter
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals(appId='{{blueprintAppId}}')/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal
Authorization: Bearer {{deleteBlueprintToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

